68,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"},{"id":23100309084479,"type":"genre","name":"glam","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":97,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"}],"album_genres":[{"id":238796249276494,"type":"genre","name":"Britpop","n":1},{"id":234622321273601,"type":"genre","name":"alternative pop","n":1},{"id":210192360016800,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Rock","n":1},{"id":117363531556446,"type":"genre","name":"Jazz-Rock","n":1},{"id":102845406900443,"type":"genre","name":"Pop Punk","n":1}],"labels":[],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[{"id":193634530822272,"name":"Brit-pop y post-pop","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1990,"end":2001,"desc":"Como tantas veces, el fenómeno más publicitado es el menos interesante: un «brit-pop» de grupos terriblemente parecidos y tediosos, sin apenas imaginación. Lo anticipan Lightning Seeds, La's, Teenage Fanclub y Heavenly; estalla con Boo Radleys, Blur (Parklife) y Oasis (el «farol» que mejor personifica la moda). Suede y el glam-pop (Super Furry Animals, Placebo), las excepciones de High Llamas (Hawaii) y Supergrass, el revival mod (Ocean Colour Scene, Wildhearts), Elastica, Sleeper, las Spice Girls; Trembling Blue Stars, Tindersticks, Delgados. El post-pop de Radiohead, «la banda más publicitada y sobrevalorada de la década», cuyo OK Computer es una obra maestra del falso vanguardismo; Coldplay, Travis.","color":"#f472b6","family":"Pop, power-pop y synth-pop","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#britpop"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":13065386424228,"artist":"Placebo","artist_id":212519933922739,"title":"Placebo","year":1996,"ess":0,"yt":"MUGG0AF5IJM","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Brit-pop y post-pop","scene_id":193634530822272,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#britpop","chapters":["Sección 6.11"],"pages":[[1,271,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":271,"text":"…offered an original take on glam-pop on Suede (1993), one that inspired bands such as the Super Furry Animals, with Fuzzy Logic (1996), and Placebo , with Placebo (1996). The Smiths were a strong influence on the Sundays, Echobelly, Gene. The exceptions to the rule of mediocrity were few. Former Microdisney's…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Emergence During Britpop's Decline (1996)","body":"Placebo was one of the new bands that appeared in 1996, at a time when the British market was changing and Britpop was beginning to wane. \"en 1996 y salía a mandas como placebo\"","year":1996,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"El BRIT POP como negocio discográfico","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uIx0P0TssZ0"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Contemporary Glam Trappings","body":"Placebo is listed as an act exhibiting \"Glam trappings\" in their music and visual style, demonstrating glam's ongoing influence in later decades. \"and Placebo.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Surprising History of Glam Rock","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=blDNqVFheAw"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Inspired by Joy Division's Sound","body":"The British band Placebo was deeply inspired by Joy Division's guitar sound and many other aspects of their music, not just Ian Curtis's influence. \"Tenemos a Placébo, ya en el Rino Nido también, que se inspiró muchísimo también. El sonido de guitarra y en muchas cosas de lo que sería Joy Division no solo en Cortes.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Especial JOY DIVISION: 4. La banda tras el final","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r5DddiWrUbA"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Partial Resistance to Spotify","body":"Placebo, an \"indie\" group, was initially a significant opponent of Spotify. While shared rights prevented them from removing their entire discography, they initially refused to publish the part they had complete control over. Ultimately, they surrendered and made their music available. \"Los Blackis o placebo que también han sido grandes enemigos. Spotify que no podían quitar toda su discografía por temas de derechos compartidos, pero la parte en la que tenían total control de su discografía, así se negaban a publicarla, que también al final se acababan rindiendo de la como, ¡Mira, tomadla porque esto no puede enfrentarme a ti!\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Artistas que no están en Spotify y por qué","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RQYV60lqU8Y"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Production by Alan Moulder","body":"Alan Moulder was a producer for Placebo. \"fue productor de placebo.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Mellon Collie and The Infinite Sadness: ¿Por qué suena diferente?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mYPtjJN11zU"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Remaining Members","body":"Stephan Molesal is mentioned as the bassist and one of the only remaining members of Placebo, alongside Brian Molko. \"Stephan Molesal es el bajo de plazivo es el único miembro que queda de plazivo junta Brian Molko.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Mejores discos del 2017","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T34CwsFmXpI"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Shoegaze Influence","body":"The band remained very inspired by shoegaze music, demonstrating the genre's continued, albeit sometimes \"reduced,\" influence on later artists. \"casi placebo siguió muy inspirado más en su vez.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"DREAM POP y SHOEGAZE. Diferencias entre ellos.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=75cEjgxTR3U"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[{"kind":"concert","title":"Project Revolution Tour (2007-2008)","body":null,"year":2007,"extra":nu